{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition","id":1560610,"title":"Thoughts for 3rd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-13T23:40:30-07:00","id":1560610,"title":"Thoughts for 3rd Edition","content":"After hearing that a 3rd edition is in the works, I thought I would throw out my thoughts on what might make this launch a better one from my perspective as a customer. I don't pretend to speak for anyone else, this is just me riffing.<br /> <br /> 1. Release the three core books first, and THEN start adding Companions, Dragons, Pantheons, and so on.This will eliminate the two biggest problems I had with the current edition. First, you couldn't play all the way from Origin to God until 8 years had passed and all the books were out. And second, every expansion was released when different core books were out, so they didn't contain all the rules needed for playing at higher power levels, and those had to be added on later.<br /> <br /> 2. Come up with a game world that fits the game premise. The current &quot;our world, but not&quot; makes absolutely no sense, and requires everyone to come up with their own take before they can even start up a campaign.<br /> <br /> 3. Include more and better examples of character creation, skill use, and combat for newcomers to the game. Hopefully, having it fit into the fully developed OP system will make things go more smoothly, but it still helps to have clear directions on how to do things.<br /> <br /> There might be more, but those are the biggest issues I hope will be addressed. Any other thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T02:41:39-07:00","id":1560614,"title":"","content":"Fix so the rules for armour is the same between characters and opponents. Was a problem when you had soft/hard armour for characters and then just armour for opponents, as there were rules that behaved differently on what type of armour it was. <br /> <br /> Definitively agree with the need for more and better examples.<br /> <br /> I like the flavour texts that were for some of the boons. Have that for all of them as they give ideas on how they can be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28936-ulfgeir","name":"Ulfgeir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T08:21:26-07:00","id":1560618,"title":"","content":"Playable counts. We need interpretations of mythology suitable for RPGs. Some people were arguing for <b>HUMAN SACRIFICE </b>on these boards! This is a game. Respect for other people's cultures is good, but it's just a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T15:21:01-07:00","id":1560625,"title":"","content":"Agreed on point number one. It's been frustrating to have to consult three different books just for one tier of play because the necessary rules for a given splat (in this case, Dragons) had to be divided into so many different sections.<br /> <br /> Point three I wouldn't mind at all, though I didn't as much problems with it in that regard.<br /> <br /> Point number two I'm unsure about, simply because how are you defining a proper &quot;world that fits the premise?&quot; What in your eyes is a world that suits the gameline best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T23:56:55-07:00","id":1560632,"title":"","content":"I have never agreed with &quot;the world is the same as our world, in spite of centuries of active worship of other Pantheons, all of whom actively influence their followers and the world itself, to the point of literal manifestation&quot;. Non-human races exist, Atlantis was real, multiple afterlives are a thing, the dead can be raised, and yet everything is the same as in our own, mana-dead, religiously stifled, culturally oppressed reality? I just can't get behind that at all. I know it opens a huge can of worms, but honestly, 1st edition's &quot;the Gods were off the board until the titans started to reawaken&quot; was a better explanation of why everything was the same until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T03:19:50-07:00","id":1560633,"title":"","content":"Why not simply say, this isn't our world but a world close to it. And suggest that Fate kept it close to a world like our own world for their reasons. No real explanation but enough for a game and it let's each Storyteller spin details their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T06:43:38-07:00","id":1560634,"title":"","content":"I suspect that's what they will end up doing, for convenience and to avoid offense to anyone. I just don't think the world would be as it is, if the many deities of Scion were as tangible and active as the game postulates. It never sat right with me. But the other points I made are certainly more important in the long run, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T11:21:56-07:00","id":1560639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition#post1560610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Release the three core books first, and THEN start adding Companions, Dragons, Pantheons, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agree on this! The power scaling for the alternative playstyle options hits the ceiling faster, because it's waiting on the core game to expand the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition#post1560610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Come up with a game world that fits the game premise. The current &quot;our world, but not&quot; makes absolutely no sense, and requires everyone to come up with their own take before they can even start up a campaign.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also agree on this. It's ridiculous to think the various pantheons would respect human agency and allow them to govern themselves without interference. Some pantheons viewed humans as literal slaves, who only existed to serve their whims. While other pantheons depicted their gods as living forces of nature, that mortals had to placate in order to keep their more destructive behavior to a minimum.<br /> <br /> I understand that the writers might feel scared about offending pagan faiths, by depicting their gods in less than favorable lights. But you can't just cherry pick which part of the mythology you want to celebrate and ignore the rest.<br /> <br /> If you want a game set in the real world, where you're playing as children / agents of classic, mythological figures, then go all in with it. Don't half ass the setting, because you were raised by Disney. (Even though Hercules was a great movie).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition#post1560610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Include more and better examples of character creation, skill use, and combat for newcomers to the game. Hopefully, having it fit into the fully developed OP system will make things go more smoothly, but it still helps to have clear directions on how to do things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The game actively encourages players to come up with their own Gifts, Knacks, est. So this is also something that I agree could use some expansion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 06-15-2026, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T14:34:39-07:00","id":1560641,"title":"","content":"There was a Superhero game <b>Wild Talents </b>that had rules for customizing the setting along several vectors. A little of that has been tried. A more coherent version with details on why it matters might be worth pursuing. <br /> <br /> Also, while more pantheons detailed for the players is a good thing, it might be useful to note how compatible a given pantheon is with either the modern world or the existence of other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T18:54:40-07:00","id":1560663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560641#post1560641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a Superhero game <b>Wild Talents </b>that had rules for customizing the setting along several vectors. A little of that has been tried. A more coherent version with details on why it matters might be worth pursuing.<br /> <br /> Also, while more pantheons detailed for the players is a good thing, it might be useful to note how compatible a given pantheon is with either the modern world or the existence of other pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was first edition, but didn't they have a Ragnarok book that presented the Aesir / Norse as being the only pantheon in the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T22:13:26-07:00","id":1560668,"title":"","content":"Incorporate Myth Levels from <b>Mysteries of the World</b> into the core book, with the advice for Iron Evidence being applied for groups that like the \u201cOur World, But Not\u201d approach, and something between Heroic and Gold Evidence for a setting where the existence of the Pantheons has significantly altered history. <br /> <br /> Either publish a core book that allows for everything from Origin to God levels of play, or publish the Tier books (Hero, Demigod, and God) back to back. <b>Scion: God</b> 3e should include rules for character creation for <b>God</b>-level characters, instead of shunting that to a supplement. <br /> <br /> Either incorporate the essentials of <b>Saints and Monsters</b> into the core book, or release a 3e version of it as the first book on the schedule after the core book(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T00:59:49-07:00","id":1560670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560663#post1560663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it was first edition, but didn't they have a Ragnarok book that presented the Aesir / Norse as being the only pantheon in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the more popular pantheons that's worth pursuing. Not just the Norse pantheon but the Greek and Egyptian ones are obvious choices. I think the Voudoun, Chinese, Japanese, Irish, and Hindi pantheons have enough popularity to sustain such books as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T02:47:14-07:00","id":1560672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560670#post1560670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the more popular pantheons that's worth pursuing. Not just the Norse pantheon but the Greek and Egyptian ones are obvious choices. I think the Voudoun, Chinese, Japanese, Irish, and Hindi pantheons have enough popularity to sustain such books as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember my Greek mythology correctly, they are really big on the whole tragedy narrative.<br /> <br /> And with some Heroes ascending to godhood poshumously, it's possible that dying might actually serve as a form of 'character development.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T14:12:14-07:00","id":1560720,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I want the supplements to be planned out better. A lot of the supplements always felt half-done, such as how non-human species and sorcerers had almost no info on how higher tiers differed, or even how you reached them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, titanic scions had their information and mechanics spread over about 3-4 books, each of which changed things, creating what was mostly a confusing mess where you needed 5 books just for a hero-tier character.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I really don't like how common it is to find multiple books reprinting the same mechanics, but now updated with different rules. I'm not sure how many crafting rules iterations we've had, but I'm pretty sure it's too many.<br /> <br /> Finally, I really want more support for Scions who focus more on magic, especially for combat. You can sort of use weapon tags to hack together magic wands and such, but otherwise you're mostly stuck spending a legend to gain a basic magic attack for a scene. In general Scion really does not seem to want you to be magical in the lower levels, beyond your two boons and the occasional marvel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T16:12:37-07:00","id":1560727,"title":"","content":"Kenod has a point both on organization of data and magic. If small amounts of data are needed in several places, okay. But there should be one main source with all the data on major topics. The Titanic scion book (to use Kenod's example) should have <b>ALL</b> the data on Titanic scions. White Wolf/Onyx Path has had this problem before. Most of the official Revenant families weren't in the main Ghouls book nor the revised edition of that book. That sort of thing shouldn't happen in a 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> Magic is just not given the time of day in this game. Becoming a powerful spellcaster just isn't supported. Also, several mystic traditions in the real world teach that humans can ascend to Godhood through Occult study and practice. A non Scion human can barely do anything in a reasonable amount of time to be a serious threat to other mortals let alone scions and gods. There are figures in the Hindu myths who become more powerful than the gods through ritual performance. Nothing even close shows up in Scion. Kenod has a point, Magic by Scions, gods, mythic beings, and mortals, needs a lot of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-23-2026, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T10:49:30-07:00","id":1560759,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of rough areas that need work. but ultimately, since the heavy lifting of developing the foundations of the system has already been done (we have 2e to build from, and the difference shouldn't be anything like the step from 1e to 2e was), it shouldn't be impossible to put out the core books, containing all the needed mechanics, and THEN add complete supplements on the Titans/Mythos/Dragons/Sorcerers, expanded Pantheons, world books, and so on. The other main RPG companies follow the &quot;core then expand&quot; model (DnD, Pathfinder, Call of Cthulhu, Vampire, etc), so it isn't outrageous to ask that OP follows that example. I can say that I won't support a piecemeal approach at all - I got burned with 2e taking so long to get the core books out, and won't do that again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T03:42:13-07:00","id":1560776,"title":"","content":"Hmm, at the very least, what I don't want is an Origin book. Or more specifically, I don't want to have to wait a year to be able to actually play a Scion, instead of just random civilians.<br /> <br /> Beyond that though, yeah, a focused road map for the core books would be very much appreciated, with no supplements being placed in-between until that's finished. I can accept the companion books being in-between, but no more half-finished splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T21:29:10-07:00","id":1560875,"title":"","content":"I agree that history in the scion world should have been more changed. For example in our games, the Aztec empire never fell and beat the conquistadors back with blood magic. They now rule most of middle America. And north America is a mixed state with both the native American and new Yankee gods at the helm as the native Americans never where beaten like in our world. There never was a trail of tears. And elsewhere in the world should also be more changes. You can keep the base but change the details , for example keep the British empire but instead of Christianity its the tuatha de dannan who controll the British empire and the British monarch is their chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28820-akhelos","name":"Akhelos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T01:11:08-07:00","id":1560877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akhelos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560875#post1560875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that history in the scion world should have been more changed. For example in our games, the Aztec empire never fell and beat the conquistadors back with blood magic. They now rule most of middle America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in order for the Aztec pantheon to survive, the empire would have had to win the conflict.<br /> <br /> The whole reason why they performed human sacrifices in the first place, is because they believed it was necessary to stop the world form ending.<br /> <br /> If the conquistadores had won, and put a stop to the practice, only to learn the world was perfectly fine without needing to cut people's hearts out, the blow it would have done to the Aztec faith would have been catastrophic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akhelos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560875#post1560875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They now rule most of middle America. And north America is a mixed state with both the native American and new Yankee gods at the helm as the native Americans never where beaten like in our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems strange that a pantheon, who's PSP is supposed to focus on medicine, would be wiped out by diseases the Europeans introduced.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akhelos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560875#post1560875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And elsewhere in the world should also be more changes. You can keep the base but change the details , for example keep the British empire but instead of Christianity its the tuatha de dannan who controll the British empire and the British monarch is their chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The British dug too deeply in the hills of Ireland, and pissed off the Fey!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T07:48:05-07:00","id":1560884,"title":"","content":"As much as I want further expand on how different The World would be due to the &quot;All Myths Are True&quot; setting... Yeah, I can see that not happening. The history of the World's probably for the Storyguides to decide for their own game since a singular &quot;canonical&quot; answer will probably rub people wrong one way or another because they will each have their own idea on what's <i>supposed</i> to happen. And that's ultimately going to result in a setting completely unrecognizeable from our own that the developers might as well just invent something from the whole cloth and dump the characters in. And <i>some of us</i> are interested in player modern-day demigods in the actual modern world, not Generic Fantasy World #2599825295 with a completely original map, countries, cultures, geopolitical dynamics, etc., but the Gods remain as it for no explainable reasons.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, but the Gods being real should mean [particular tragedy] shouldn't happen!&quot; Religious people still exist. They existed then and they exist now. Despite all the tragedies that have happened, sometimes to them, their people, and their cultures and countries, their faith still remain and they still believe there's a God (or Gods, or Ancestors, or Higher Beings, etc.), the God's existence is stronger than anything science could prove, and such tragedies still happened despite the God's existence. If they could wrap their heads around that idea and continue to live their lives, then you could sustain your disbelief long enough for a session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akhelos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1560875#post1560875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can keep the base but change the details , for example keep the British empire but instead of Christianity its the tuatha de dannan who controll the British empire and the British monarch is their chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tuatha got their asses handed to them by the Milesians to the point they had to relinquish the upper half of Ireland to the mortals and retreat back to the underground sidhe mounds and the Otherworld. They can't even keep control of an island country and you really think they could have a global empire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T12:22:05-07:00","id":1560894,"title":"","content":"This is why I think the 1st edition history worked better: the Gods were off playing chess or something, and the world went on as we know it, until the Titans broke free. Now the Gods are back, setting their Scions to battle the Titans and their minions. The world can then change going from that point forward. The dominance of a handful of faiths that we see in our world really doesn't make senseif all the other religions are still active and powerful; without a major &quot;alternate timeline&quot;, the &quot;All Myths are True&quot; tagline doesn't really work.<br /> That said - I just want the freaking rulebooks all to be available so I can work out a campaign from Hero to God, as the game was intended to allow, without an 8-year wait and a lot of incomplete supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T01:12:52-07:00","id":1561050,"title":"","content":"I'd want Scion 3e to include an Abrahamic Pantheon in the base core Pantheons. Use Archangels instead of Gods if they have to. The writers keep saying that they shirk around the arguably single most influential mythology in the modern world in order to &quot;avoid offending people&quot;, but they apparently didn't have that problem with Hinduism, Shinto and Buddhism.<br /> <br /> I also have a pet peeve with the Gaulish Titans. The ones from <b>Titans Rising</b> are complete and utter fanfiction, and they didn't even mention Orgos, who was supposed to be THE Gaulish Titan back in <b>Mysteries of the World</b>! I also hate how Sorcerers are almost treated like an afterthought, and how they seemingly completely forgot about Denizens after <b>Player's Guide - Saints &amp; Monsters</b>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and the whole thing about the Orisha don\u2019t have Titans? That\u2019s like, factually wrong to real-world Yoruba religion? Here\u2019s my proof: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajogun\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajogun</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 06-27-2026, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T11:24:43-07:00","id":1561057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561050#post1561050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here\u2019s my proof: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajogun\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajogun</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this it's fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T16:07:48-07:00","id":1561064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561050#post1561050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd want Scion 3e to include an Abrahamic Pantheon in the base core Pantheons. Use Archangels instead of Gods if they have to. The writers keep saying that they shirk around the arguably single most influential mythology in the modern world in order to &quot;avoid offending people&quot;, but they apparently didn't have that problem with Hinduism, Shinto and Buddhism.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the rules on the Scion Community Content Style Guide said not to use &quot;monotheistic&quot; religions in Scion. They don't outright said it, but it's pretty much referring to the Abrahamic religions specifically, especially with the addition of the Orishas in Hero and the Yazata in Companion. IIRC some of the developers mentioned on Discord years ago that one of the main reasons why they don't want to do an Abrahamic Pantheon is they don't want to present it as a Big Happy Family by lumping three religions with history of bad blood, discrimination, and genocides under one umbrella. Sooo, yeah. Unless there are Christian, Jewish, and Muslim writers working in tandem, I don't think we'll get an official Abrahamic Pantheon any time soon...<br /> <br /> But hey, at least we can still convert yours to 3E!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561050#post1561050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a pet peeve with the Gaulish Titans. The ones from <b>Titans Rising</b> are complete and utter fanfiction, and they didn't even mention Orgos, who was supposed to be THE Gaulish Titan back in <b>Mysteries of the World</b>!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Honestly I'd prefer if the Nemetondevos just flat-out don't have Titans of their own and instead just targeting the Theoi and their Scions, especially those born of their Roman Mantles. Instead of a Titanomachy, the Gaulish Gods are much more invested in an Olympiamachy. Really emphasizing on the idea that Titanhood can be as political and perspective-based as it is cosmological.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T02:32:43-07:00","id":1561070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the rules on the Scion Community Content Style Guide said not to use &quot;monotheistic&quot; religions in Scion. They don't outright said it, but it's pretty much referring to the Abrahamic religions specifically, especially with the addition of the Orishas in Hero and the Yazata in Companion. IIRC some of the developers mentioned on Discord years ago that one of the main reasons why they don't want to do an Abrahamic Pantheon is they don't want to present it as a Big Happy Family by lumping three religions with history of bad blood, discrimination, and genocides under one umbrella. Sooo, yeah. Unless there are Christian, Jewish, and Muslim writers working in tandem, I don't think we'll get an official Abrahamic Pantheon any time soon... </div> </div> </div>I'll also add that there are some pretty major theological differences that are sort of irreconcilable, and also quite core to each of the religions. For instance, the status of Jesus as son of God would either make Christianity the right interpretation, and Judaism and Islam false, or opposite. And that's not getting into questions such as if Muhammed was a prophet or not, which is another nice theological time bomb.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's also the question of how to work an omnipotent being that basically breaks the fundamental rules of Scion into the setting, or, if you don't, explaining why they aren't relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T02:50:42-07:00","id":1561071,"title":"","content":"You also have the problem that if one solitary god is starting to get a bit too powerful, other pantheons might feel treatened and decide to take action. It is one thing to have people believe in a different set of gods, but when said solitary god tries to impose that the others do not exist, you got a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28936-ulfgeir","name":"Ulfgeir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T04:08:10-07:00","id":1561073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kenod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561070#post1561070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, there's also the question of how to work an omnipotent being that basically breaks the fundamental rules of Scion into the setting, or, if you don't, explaining why they aren't relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, such concept of an all-powerful supreme deity isn't something exclusive to YHWH. The Yazata claim the same thing with Ahura Mazda, the Orisha with Olorun, the Loa with Bondye, and the Deva with the likes of Shiva, Vishnu, and Shakti (whose incarnations include Parvati, Durga, Kali, Lakshmi, and Sarasvati), and those Deva are all available as divine parent options since Origin. Even Azathoth is available as a patron should you wish to implement Masks of the Mythos into your game. And those are only the first Gods that pop up in my head.<br /> <br /> If YHWH is &quot;too powerful&quot; to be in Scion, then all those other Gods shouldn't be either since saying they are anything <i>but</i> all-powerful kinda go against their respective mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T10:41:42-07:00","id":1561102,"title":"","content":"Except that the world we live in has allowed the belief in one particular deity (arguably with a few different names) to eclipse all the others. If &quot;All Myths are True&quot;, then Ahura Mazda, Tezcatlipoca, El, Ra, and any other Creation-making Gods/Goddesses are equal to that one being - so in a game universe where they are all active, with Scions, manifestations, and political maneuvering, how do you say it still all came out to equal the same world we live in now? Maybe some folks are okay with that, but it just doesn't sit right with me. And at the very least, once you start a campaign, and the PCs are doing stuff against gods and monsters, the status quo shouldn't survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T05:15:30-07:00","id":1561125,"title":"","content":"When I saw that Scion is getting a Third Edition so soon I fumed a bit because I already bought the last book for the Titans path and now I have to start all over again. Personally, I would like the Dragon book and Masks of the Mythos to have a Third Ed. makeover to transfer over properly. As for the &quot;no Christianity&quot; rule, there is an alternative. Before the Council of Nicea codified the Bible, Christianity was more mystical. There were the Gnostics who believed that everyone had a connection to the Monad as long as they remembered that they could. There was a whole mythology attached to it depending on which version you chose: With Sophia and Christ being zygonistic Aeons in service to the One and that Sophia created Yaldabroth(?) who did the Genesis thing being totally ignorant about the Pleroma and his Archons who monitored the world. Then in another branch, there's Abraxas of whom even the gods feared because of his status of both Good and Evil, being neutral to both. In Scion, would Abraxas be considered a trinity of God, Titan, and Dragon? Plus, there the Ophidians who believed that Christ was the snake in Eden who tried to awaken Adam and Eve, but failed when there awakening threw them down into the frequency of Fear and Shame. Perhaps we should have another thread about this. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T06:44:56-07:00","id":1561133,"title":"","content":"I think that at this point you're getting more into Mage territory than Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T23:40:27-07:00","id":1561152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kenod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561133#post1561133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that at this point you're getting more into Mage territory than Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bare in mind that the final capstone for all Purviews in 1st edition was literally described as the player being able to seize narrative control of the scene from the ST.<br /> <br /> As well as granting you the ability to do things which were logically impossible. Such as using the purview of FIRE to burn the Greater Titan of Fire.<br /> <br /> For context, the Great Titan of Fire is supposed to be the living concept of fire itself. So you're using fire to burn fire!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T05:34:27-07:00","id":1561157,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd like to see them keep up the theme of Supernatural Paths, but introducing some Titanspawn options.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> <b>Giants / Jotun</b> (prominently featured in the battle of Ragnarok)<br /> <br /> <b>Oni / Yokai </b>(honestly surprised they aren't an option already)<br /> <br /> <b>Yaoguai </b>(animals who awakened and became demons)<br /> <br /> <b>Nephilim</b> (biblical version)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T02:39:13-07:00","id":1561509,"title":"","content":"Personally I would just avoid having a &quot;this is how the World is&quot; section at all, and make the Myth Level dials the default, so everyone can build the setting to their personal liking.<br /> <br /> I kind of like the semi-covert Masquerade from 1e, but it would need to be done better. The 2e setting where stuff like &quot;Oh, everyone knows Astarte is real, look, here's her instagram account&quot; doesn't sit right with me at all. It's kind of a Superheroes without costumes setting as it is, which is cool but not what I'm after. I know there's probably a commentary to be made somewhere about big name superhero teams being modern Pantheons, which reminds me I need to read Grant Morrison's book Supergods, but nevertheless. <br /> <br /> I would have the gods be absent because of a cold war between pantheons, where they haven't been meddling in the World in obvious ways to avoid setting off their rivals. And I'd have the Titanomachy explicitly take advantage of the fact that the gods were watching each other, not their &quot;defeated&quot; enemies.<br /> <br /> I personally would also just have Dragons be Gods or Titans if they're powerful enough, and regular monsters if they aren't. I feel like the setting has tripped over itself to try and make the &quot;all myths are true and accurate&quot; thing happen, while then also making Dragons a Secret Cohesive Third Faction in a way that isn't really accurate to anything.<br /> Don't get me wrong, it's NEAT and I'm not dragging the people who wrote or enjoy it, it's just not what I would have done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":12975,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","user":"Zealot_Vedas","date":".  clarity and expansion to avoid doubleposting 07-09-2026, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T07:46:46-07:00","id":1561516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561509#post1561509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would just avoid having a &quot;this is how the World is&quot; section at all, and make the Myth Level dials the default, so everyone can build the setting to their personal liking.<br /> <br /> I kind of like the semi-covert Masquerade from 1e, but it would need to be done better. The 2e setting where stuff like &quot;Oh, everyone knows Astarte is real, look, here's her instagram account&quot; doesn't sit right with me at all. It's kind of a Superheroes without costumes setting as it is, which is cool but not what I'm after. I know there's probably a commentary to be made somewhere about big name superhero teams being modern Pantheons, which reminds me I need to read Grant Morrison's book Supergods, but nevertheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mythological heroes act more like a band of roving murder hobos, than they do super heroes.<br /> <br /> Cu Chulainn, for example, slaughtered his way through an entire castle, when he found out the king had no intention of allowing him to marry his daughter.<br /> <br /> Hercules was cursed with psychotic rage, that lead to him being responsible for the death of both his family, as well as his best friend.<br /> <br /> Odin and Thor were taken prisoner by the dwarves when they accidentally killed their prince who was taking the form of an otter at the time. Rather than agreeing to pay the ransom in an honest attempt to make amends, Loki decided to fill the prince's pelt with cursed gold that causes the dwarves to begin murdering each other in a struggle to claim it for themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561509#post1561509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have the gods be absent because of a cold war between pantheons, where they haven't been meddling in the World in obvious ways to avoid setting off their rivals. And I'd have the Titanomachy explicitly take advantage of the fact that the gods were watching each other, not their &quot;defeated&quot; enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a conflict between the gods we have to worry about. The gods are defined by their connection to humanity, and giving them a greater sense of agency.<br /> <br /> The problem with a cold war, is that the Titans are very much different in that regard. They are defined by a complete detachment from humanity, and are dominated by the urge to fulfill their purviews.<br /> <br /> Titans and their respective Scions lack the very capacity to wage a cold war. It's like starting an open flame in the middle of the forest, and then expecting the fire will honor a civil agreement not to burn the place down.<br /> <br /> Cold Wars might be possible, if the setting takes place in a world where the Titans are still imprisoned, but trying to break free. If they're already free and roaming the land, however, there's no way in hell that anybody is keeping a lid on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even if we ignore their real life personalities and just assume the various pantheons would be cool with letting each other do their own thing... the mortals who worship them are a completely different story. History is replete with accounts of us trying to convert each other, either peacefully or at the point of a sword (or some other equivalent). As well as there being cases where rival cults try to prove which god is superior by calling out to them to perform miracles.<br /> <br /> So regardless of how much they might want to avoid drawing each other's ire, the Gods are going to be pulled into conflict with each other one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":".  Fixed a correction with the QUOTE format. 07-09-2026, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T15:18:23-07:00","id":1561574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayNg2183</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561064#post1561064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the rules on the Scion Community Content Style Guide said not to use &quot;monotheistic&quot; religions in Scion. They don't outright said it, but it's pretty much referring to the Abrahamic religions specifically, especially with the addition of the Orishas in Hero and the Yazata in Companion. IIRC some of the developers mentioned on Discord years ago that one of the main reasons why they don't want to do an Abrahamic Pantheon is they don't want to present it as a Big Happy Family by lumping three religions with history of bad blood, discrimination, and genocides under one umbrella. Sooo, yeah. Unless there are Christian, Jewish, and Muslim writers working in tandem, I don't think we'll get an official Abrahamic Pantheon any time soon...<br /> <br /> But hey, at least we can still convert yours to 3E!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m going to sounds extremely conceited for saying this\u2026 but the very fact that I\u2019ve been able to pull it off without presenting as a Big Happy Family (I went out of my way to emphasize the fractiousness of the Abrahamic religions as a core part of the Pantheon\u2019s identity) means that the writers can to. They\u2019ve got no excuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561509#post1561509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would just avoid having a &quot;this is how the World is&quot; section at all, and make the Myth Level dials the default, so everyone can build the setting to their personal liking.<br /> <br /> I kind of like the semi-covert Masquerade from 1e, but it would need to be done better. The 2e setting where stuff like &quot;Oh, everyone knows Astarte is real, look, here's her instagram account&quot; doesn't sit right with me at all. It's kind of a Superheroes without costumes setting as it is, which is cool but not what I'm after. I know there's probably a commentary to be made somewhere about big name superhero teams being modern Pantheons, which reminds me I need to read Grant Morrison's book Supergods, but nevertheless.<br /> <br /> I would have the gods be absent because of a cold war between pantheons, where they haven't been meddling in the World in obvious ways to avoid setting off their rivals. And I'd have the Titanomachy explicitly take advantage of the fact that the gods were watching each other, not their &quot;defeated&quot; enemies.<br /> <br /> I personally would also just have Dragons be Gods or Titans if they're powerful enough, and regular monsters if they aren't. I feel like the setting has tripped over itself to try and make the &quot;all myths are true and accurate&quot; thing happen, while then also making Dragons a Secret Cohesive Third Faction in a way that isn't really accurate to anything.<br /> Don't get me wrong, it's NEAT and I'm not dragging the people who wrote or enjoy it, it's just not what I would have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally like the no-Masquerade &quot;modernized Gods&quot; thing from 2e; I found it a novel take on urban fantasy, while Masquerade settings are already dime-a-dozen. I agree with you about Dragons, though: the Dragon books read to me like someone on the writing team hijacking Scion to platform their original work without doing the actual effort of building an entire setting and rule system from scratch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T18:35:54-07:00","id":1561578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561574#post1561574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m going to sounds extremely conceited for saying this\u2026 but the very fact that I\u2019ve been able to pull it off without presenting as a Big Happy Family (I went out of my way to emphasize the fractiousness of the Abrahamic religions as a core part of the Pantheon\u2019s identity) means that the writers can to. They\u2019ve got no excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you made one to sell to a general audience and then had to deal with the reactions to it? Because there's a significant different calculus for profession products than fan ones.<br /> <br /> And no offense, but as a practicing Jew? I've never seen an attempt to do an &quot;Abrahamic&quot; &quot;pantheon&quot; that doesn't come off as wildly misinformed fan-wank. Mostly because you need to draw 99% of your inspiration from apocrypha over scripture (or decide that Ethiopian Orthodox is the correct version of scripture). &quot;Biblically accurate angels&quot; just look like humans. The Internet meme entirely comes from post-Exilic stories that never made it into the vast majority of canons. Biblical Nephilim? Again, accurate to what? Two (maybe three) sentences that tell you nothing (again, unless you dip into the Book of the Watchers)? <br /> <br /> If you want to actually stay true to Scion's whole premise... you should be making a Western Semitic Pantheon that combines the Ugaritic, Assyrian, Canaanite, and pre-Excilic Israelite practices we have tons of actual evidence to reconstruct. The Divine Council is actually a structure of pantheon that isn't as prominent in Scion because the members of it are all patron deities of individual people-groups with lots of overlap in portfolios instead of each filling a cosmological niche and the differences stem from who they were worshiped by and what that land was like. You can leave it up to individual groups if you want to keep the Pantheon members that were diminished in reality through wars and conquests as still being around and active, or if only one of them managed to survive all of that with serious power and has claimed the leadership of the Pantheon for themself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T19:00:47-07:00","id":1561579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561574#post1561574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally like the no-Masquerade &quot;modernized Gods&quot; thing from 2e; I found it a novel take on urban fantasy, while Masquerade settings are already dime-a-dozen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly why I think Myth Levels should be baked into the 3e core book, not a supplement. Those solved my issues with 2e's setting in one stroke, and with them we can all have the version we like. Which, frankly, we would probably do anyway, but Myth Levels are a convenient framework for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T06:42:01-07:00","id":1561600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561574#post1561574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m going to sounds extremely conceited for saying this\u2026 but the very fact that I\u2019ve been able to pull it off without presenting as a Big Happy Family (I went out of my way to emphasize the fractiousness of the Abrahamic religions as a core part of the Pantheon\u2019s identity) means that the writers can to. They\u2019ve got no excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, &quot;They've got no excuse&quot; makes it sound more like you're requiring them to include the pantheon and that it's an expected part of Scion, which it really shouldn't be. Beyond that, the issue is that, even if <i>you</i> managed to get it right, the OPP writers will be well aware that they might not do so. In which case they'll get the backlash. Realistically speaking, there's absolutely no reason to run that risk to include something many people might not even care that much about. They also only have a single shot at getting it right, and getting it right for everyone (not just the people interested in buying an Abrehamic fan supplement). And, lets face it, everyone knows that even the best writers get it wrong at times (just look at Dragon and its companion book).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T00:22:44-07:00","id":1561620,"title":"","content":"Other issues you encounter with including Abrahamic Pantheons; 1) You immediately start the whole &quot;Isn't capital 'G' the ultimate deity? How dare you show other Gods having equal power!&quot; debate. 2) You open yourself up to the more violently fanatical of worshippers who often take umbrage at &quot;misrepresentation&quot;. 3) You have to decide which interpretations are going to inform your pantheon, and no matter what, someone will be angry. It isn't worth the hassle, frankly, and I can see why they avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T17:10:30-07:00","id":1561644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561620#post1561620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other issues you encounter with including Abrahamic Pantheons; 1) You immediately start the whole &quot;Isn't capital 'G' the ultimate deity? How dare you show other Gods having equal power!&quot; debate. 2) You open yourself up to the more violently fanatical of worshippers who often take umbrage at &quot;misrepresentation&quot;. 3) You have to decide which interpretations are going to inform your pantheon, and no matter what, someone will be angry. It isn't worth the hassle, frankly, and I can see why they avoid it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think there's a way of working around that in an official published product. BUT, deities and pantheons are probably the easiest thing to homebrew in Scion, so I think the solution if you want to include any of the big Monotheistic religions is just to make them for your home table in a way everyone present is comfortable with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T00:42:40-07:00","id":1561647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561644#post1561644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I don't think there's a way of working around that in an official published product. BUT, deities and pantheons are probably the easiest thing to homebrew in Scion, so I think the solution if you want to include any of the big Monotheistic religions is just to make them for your home table in a way everyone present is comfortable with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, homebrew or fan supplements are definitely the best solution here, allows everyone to use the interpretation they like and which fits their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T03:13:42-07:00","id":1561651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayNg2183</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561064#post1561064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the rules on the Scion Community Content Style Guide said not to use &quot;monotheistic&quot; religions in Scion. They don't outright said it, but it's pretty much referring to the Abrahamic religions specifically, especially with the addition of the Orishas in Hero and the Yazata in Companion. IIRC some of the developers mentioned on Discord years ago that one of the main reasons why they don't want to do an Abrahamic Pantheon is they don't want to present it as a Big Happy Family by lumping three religions with history of bad blood, discrimination, and genocides under one umbrella. Sooo, yeah. Unless there are Christian, Jewish, and Muslim writers working in tandem, I don't think we'll get an official Abrahamic Pantheon any time soon...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They may not have explicitly came right out and said it, but it was blatantly obvious that Aten was meant to serve as the Abrahamic God in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> He's the Greater Titan of Light, with even Legendary beings struggling to gaze upon his full glory.<br /> <br /> He claims to be the only true God in existence, while denouncing everyone else as false idols.<br /> <br /> His Titanspawn take the form of angels.<br /> <br /> He turns his worshipers into suicide bombers, who shout <i>&quot;Submit to Aten!&quot;</i> right before they explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T20:00:38-07:00","id":1562136,"title":"","content":"This may be more subjective, others may not have as much issue with it, but I'd like 3rd edition's progression through the myth levels to feel a bit more consistent. It kind of felt like it was several different games under one banner.<br /> I'd also like the rules to be a bit more specific, because I remember a lot of stuff feeling kind of vague when I read through it. Admittedly, it's been a bit and I'm due for a re-read before I could really elaborate on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T14:15:05-07:00","id":1562374,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the Epic Stats need to be fully brought back. Yes you can be as strong as Hercules or Thor, as enduring as Oshun or Atlas, or as lithe and agile as the Handsome Monkey King or Hermes. But what about as beautiful as Krishna or Aphrodite, as charismatic as Lugh or Frey, as Composed as Athena or the August Elder of Jade, as Tricky as Anansi or Loki, as intelligent as Isis or Odin, as mentally quick as Thoth or Hermes, as determined as Vishnu or Oshun. <br /> <br /> I get the Mental and Social Epic stats are trickier to use in play, but they are useful. And Epic Beauty/Ugliness fits many deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-31-2026, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T14:37:08-07:00","id":1562377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1562374#post1562374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that the Epic Stats need to be fully brought back. Yes you can be as strong as Hercules or Thor, as enduring as Oshun or Atlas, or as lithe and agile as the Handsome Monkey King or Hermes. But what about as beautiful as Krishna or Aphrodite, as charismatic as Lugh or Frey, as Composed as Athena or the August Elder of Jade, as Tricky as Anansi or Loki, as intelligent as Isis or Odin, as mentally quick as Thoth or Hermes, as determined as Vishnu or Oshun.<br /> <br /> I get the Mental and Social Epic stats are trickier to use in play, but they are useful. And Epic Beauty/Ugliness fits many deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently we did get Epic Charisma and Epic Perception, at least according to Pandora's Box. No clue which book they're in though.<br /> <br /> (On that note, if you make a book that collects all powers/items from all books, for the love of Djehuty please add the source and page)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T15:36:08-07:00","id":1562384,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/315311/mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the World: The Scion Second Edition Companion</a> has Epic Charisma and Perception","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T17:03:52-07:00","id":1562759,"title":"","content":"While I love Scion, second edition was an incomplete and highly cumbersome (especially for the ST) mess. It needs to be designed for streamlined, seamless play. It cannot bog the game down with too many things that the ST is expected to come up with on the fly. I have 28 years of ttrpg experience and I\u2019ve run long and highly complex games but I had to give up running the 2nd edition game of Scion I had in the works because it was crazy cumbersome for me as an ST. And too many rules were really, really vaguely written. Also, don\u2019t lose the master list of all the play test errata this time and don\u2019t ship it out until it\u2019s actually done. Scion Second Edition\u2019s backers deserved far better than what they received and unfortunately the public apology by Onyx Path did nothing to improve the game itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 08-05-2026, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T22:40:00-07:00","id":1562763,"title":"","content":"Yes, I was frustrated by getting hardcover books filled with errata and incomplete rules, and it put me off supporting later books (that, and shipping costs). They need to get it right this time; a complete set of rules to cover mortal to God, then expansion materials from there, with a cohesive and playable set of rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T14:06:26-07:00","id":1562789,"title":"","content":"2e has huge problems. I am not saying they are Shadowrun (5e or later)-level of badly written rules, but not far off. <br /> <br /> I mean the GM in the campaign I played in will restart that campaign as soon as he is finished with the current homebrewed system, and while he like the ideas the had for where it would go, and the characters, but he is seriously looking for almost any other system to use instead. We took a 6 year hiatus as we waited for the Demigod/God-level books....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28936-ulfgeir","name":"Ulfgeir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T20:13:48-07:00","id":1563485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1561578#post1561578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to actually stay true to Scion's whole premise... you should be making a Western Semitic Pantheon that combines the Ugaritic, Assyrian, Canaanite, and pre-Excilic Israelite practices we have tons of actual evidence to reconstruct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get it.<br /> Don't the Ilhm already occupy the slot as the pantheon for those cultures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T08:29:21-07:00","id":1564120,"title":"","content":"Another change I'd make to a potential Scion 3rd edition: allow Sorcerers with Purview-granting Birthrights to have access to Marvels of said Purviews, along with the Relic Motif in the case of Relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T06:31:01-07:00","id":1564166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1562759#post1562759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I love Scion, second edition was an incomplete and highly cumbersome (especially for the ST) mess. It needs to be designed for streamlined, seamless play. It cannot bog the game down with too many things that the ST is expected to come up with on the fly. I have 28 years of ttrpg experience and I\u2019ve run long and highly complex games but I had to give up running the 2nd edition game of Scion I had in the works because it was crazy cumbersome for me as an ST. And too many rules were really, really vaguely written. Also, don\u2019t lose the master list of all the play test errata this time and don\u2019t ship it out until it\u2019s actually done. Scion Second Edition\u2019s backers deserved far better than what they received and unfortunately the public apology by Onyx Path did nothing to improve the game itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever flaws 2nd edition might have had, they still made massive improvements over 1st edition.<br /> <br /> The original version of the Epic Attributes just gave you automatic successes, in addition to whatever successes you gained on dice rolls.<br /> <br /> And those automatic successes got up to bull shit levels of ridiculously over powered. Such as a whopping 42 automatic successes at 10th rank, in addition to whatever you managed to actually roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T01:33:00-07:00","id":1564174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1564166#post1564166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever flaws 2nd edition might have had, they still made massive improvements over 1st edition.<br /> <br /> The original version of the Epic Attributes just gave you automatic successes, in addition to whatever successes you gained on dice rolls.<br /> <br /> And those automatic successes got up to bull shit levels of ridiculously over powered. Such as a whopping 42 automatic successes at 10th rank, in addition to whatever you managed to actually roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yaikes! That sounds really broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28936-ulfgeir","name":"Ulfgeir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T03:45:34-07:00","id":1564180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulfgeir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1564174#post1564174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yaikes! That sounds really broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it definitely was.<br /> <br /> So broken, in fact, that many people agreed Epic Dexterity was practically the <i>&quot;Fuck you, I win&quot;</i> purview, because anybody who didn't have access to it would never be able to hit your character!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T04:43:28-07:00","id":1564184,"title":"","content":"And yet some form of <b>Epic Attribute </b>system is needed the gods show epic levels of physical, social, and mental capacities. Hermes can use disguises that Bugs Bunny couldn't get away with. Pools of automatic successes isn't the worst way to simulate this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T21:48:58-07:00","id":1564207,"title":"","content":"It also isn't the best. I'm pretty sure Feats of Scale is 2e's answer to 1e's Epic Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T16:04:45-07:00","id":1564256,"title":"","content":"Rules for more powerful denizens. For example there are rules for making fae, but you couldn't make some of the more powerful ones that show up in mythology and folklore. In Origin it says the supernatural callings should get upgrades at higher tiers, but unless they are in one of the pod products i didn't buy we never got rules for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T02:08:37-07:00","id":1564293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1564256#post1564256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules for more powerful denizens. For example there are rules for making fae, but you couldn't make some of the more powerful ones that show up in mythology and folklore. In Origin it says the supernatural callings should get upgrades at higher tiers, but unless they are in one of the pod products i didn't buy we never got rules for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, the supernatural paths had an estimated cap placed on them, based on their mythological counterparts. For example, the <i>'Cu Sith'</i> (Black Dogs) were never expected to advance beyond Origin level, because they really only serve as omens of impending doom.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cu Sith typically can not build Legend. All they can do is try to be a good dog.&quot; - Origin, page 167","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T08:11:46-07:00","id":1564300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1564293#post1564293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I recall, the supernatural paths had an estimated cap placed on them, based on their mythological counterparts. For example, the <i>'Cu Sith'</i> (Black Dogs) were never expected to advance beyond Origin level, because they really only serve as omens of impending doom.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cu Sith typically can not build Legend. All they can do is try to be a good dog.&quot; - Origin, page 167</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, but I'd argue it's also an issue caused by the paths for denizens and other supernatural figures like sorcerers being created before the later primary books were released, and thus didn't take those rules into account. The concepts work fine at Hero, but I have serious doubts as to how they scale at Demigod, and moving to God is basically a no-go.<br /> <br /> And while some might have a cap, at least sorcerers didn't, with explicit rules for how sorcery works at god tier... Which is just getting another Working type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T12:34:31-07:00","id":1564306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560610-thoughts-for-3rd-edition?p=1564293#post1564293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I recall, the supernatural paths had an estimated cap placed on them, based on their mythological counterparts. For example, the <i>'Cu Sith'</i> (Black Dogs) were never expected to advance beyond Origin level, because they really only serve as omens of impending doom.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cu Sith typically can not build Legend. All they can do is try to be a good dog.&quot; - Origin, page 167</div> </div> </div> </div>But most supernatural types in real folklore have exceptions. The Cu Sith have Black Shuck which is another level of horror. Elf maidens are no joke, but the Queen of Alfheim is a God Tier being. There's almost always a few members of any set of beings that will surprise even a demigod or higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T21:44:01-07:00","id":1564466,"title":"","content":"Hello, I'm new. I think demi-gods are a neat idea for a system so I'm planning on checking out 3E when it comes out. I will say though, I want to play as a demigod on Normal Earth. I think the fun of a modern fantasy world is how the fantasy blends with the modern. So, if you just throw out all of Earth's history, countries, and so on to let the gods play a bigger role, I don't see any reason to buy this game. I'd just blow the dust off my old D&amp;D books and roll up an Aasimar Cleric of Zeus for Forgotten Realms. The easy way would be to have hidden gods exist in a hidden society. You can also do what I've heard the last system did. Sort of soft change Earth's history, where monotheism never took off, but we still have the same history more or less. Those are... fine. I would personally want to use monotheism if I were writing a setting for this system. <br /> <br /> I remember seeing this Tiktok series a few years ago where a creator made up their own Christian faith that states the Christian god is actually Loki after he stole the title of head god from Odin. I've also seen people point out the similarities between Jesus and Dionysus. They're both sons of gods with connections to wine. There was this TV show that showed Zeus losing his eye to see the future, and specifically saw the rise of Jesus and the modern world. I really like the idea of the nature of divinity changing to match people's faith. As monotheism grows across the world it literally suppressed the pantheons. <br /> <br /> That's be an easy way to guide a metaplot too. The players have an adventure where they use their divinity to weaken the monotheist god. Players would go on an adventure to &quot;save&quot; a pantheon that would then be available as an expansion book. A higher tier would be unlocked after swaying followers away from the monotheist religions back to your pantheons. <br /> <br /> Now, would this be controversial and potentially upsetting to the real people that follow these monotheist faiths? Probably, yes. Do I feel like no matter what you do a game that touches real world religions and politics will always be labeled by those certain religious fundamentalists as promoting Satanism? Also yes. Since it's impossible to completely avoid all controversy, I think writers should look instead at what kinds of controversy to they want to steer themselves away from and towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29172-griefninja","name":"GriefNinja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}